<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>6.3.1: Dividing by Monomials</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01613</md:content-id>
    <md:title>6.3.1: Dividing by Monomials</md:title>
    <md:uuid>1fb3440c-5fce-4b0d-8ed1-3c5c4f916f88</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Warm Up Activity</title>
<para>In this unit, remember to double click on mathematical expressions/equations to enlarge, if needed.</para>
<para>In this unit, remember to double click on mathematical expressions/equations to enlarge, if needed.</para>

<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>Look at the division expression \(-54a^6b^3 \div 9a^4b^2\).</para>
    <para>Rewrite the division expression as a fraction.</para>
    <para>Write down your answer. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>Fraction form: \(\frac{-54a^6b^3}{9a^4b^2}\)</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example>

<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>Since we have a monomial divided by a monomial, we can rewrite the fraction as a product of several fractions where the factors in the numerator and denominator “match.”</para>
    <para>Write down your answer. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\(\frac{-54}{9} \cdot \frac{a^6}{a^4} \cdot \frac{b^3}{b^2}\)</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example>

<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>Now we can simplify the fraction multiplication and use the Quotient Property to divide.</para>
    <para>Write down your answer. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\(\frac{-54}{9} \cdot \frac{a^6}{a^4} \cdot \frac{b^3}{b^2} = -6 \cdot a^2 \cdot b\)
    
    So \(-54a^6b^3 \div 9a^4b^2 = -6a^2b\).
  </para>
</solution></exercise>
</example>

<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>For 4 - 6, divide a polynomial by a monomial. Divide each term of the polynomial by the monomial.</para>
    <para> Find the quotient: \((18x^3y-36xy^2) \div (-3xy)\). </para>
    <para>Write down your answer. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para><emphasis>Step 1 - </emphasis>Rewrite as a fraction.</para>
  <para> \(\frac{18x^3y-36xy^2}{-3xy}\)</para>
  <para><emphasis>Step 2 -</emphasis> Divide each term by the divisor.</para>
  <para> \(\frac{18x^3y}{-3xy}-\frac{36xy^2}{-3xy}\)</para>
  <para><emphasis>Step 3 -</emphasis> Simplify.</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example>

<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>Find the qoutient: \((48a^2b^2+ 30ab) \div (6ab)\).</para>
    <para>Write down your answer. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\(8ab+5\)</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example>

<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para> Find the quotient: \((-72g^4h^6-45g^7h^3) \div (9g^3h^3)\). </para>
    <para>Write down your answer. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\(-8gh^3-5g^4\)</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example></section>
</content>
